VALUES (626, '1', $t$ASK 626: a premise list written with bold or heading numbers is read, and a list the system cannot read is reported as LIST NOT READ, never as a forfeit$t$,
  $t$In run 42373 the defender's link round held six premises under its UNSUPPORTED-L4 PREMISES heading, numbered "**1.**" to "**6.**". Every item-head pattern wanted "1." followed by a space, so the list read as zero premises: the record said LINK ROUND FORFEITED, the judges were sent an empty ledger side, and two K-G10 items were sent to a judge against premises whose PRESSED WITH lines stood in the round text (WALL-11777 Finding 1 (a), (b), (c); W1, Wall 11804). This ASK makes every premise-list reader take one head form that accepts bold and heading numbers, and makes a list that is present but not read print LIST NOT READ, with no empty ledger, no K item and no count from it. Item 1(d), a set list form in the Oracle's prompt, was denied by the operator and is left out. (plan rev 1, ask626/w4/plan626.md md5 13acbe55; Wall 11822, 11812)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at about 04:57 to 04:59 CST 2026-11-25 on the operator's words "#626 doesn't require approval" (04:49 CST, as W4 cites them), and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11955, 11958; audit 42064). Engine 2df7f6fa to dc258730, 14 nodes, 423 nodes; the child aad0ad9c holds no list reader and was not written. What it does: one head form in every premise-list reader (optional "#" heading marks, bold marks, the number, "." or ")", optional closing bold, a space); a style lock (the first premise head sets the form of the list, and the premise count counts only heads of that form); a "### 1." item no longer ends a list body; a list with its heading present, text under it, zero premises read and no "PREMISE COUNT: 0", "none" or "no premises" line prints "LIST NOT READ: <side> -- the heading is present but the system read no premise under it; grade the list from the round text" in review_notes, the transcript and the judges' PRESSED-WITNESS LEDGER in place of LINK ROUND FORFEITED or an empty side; pwList returns null for it, so K-G10, K-P, K-R, the broken-press check, gate PL and prsUnprovenOnly raise nothing and no count comes from it. The LIST NOT READ line in the ledger is the one new text a judge sees (W1 N1); the judges' own FORFEIT rule text is untouched (W1 N2). IN PART, because it is shown offline only: t626 234 PASS, 0 FAIL with eight stored rounds; of 761 stored lists 758 read the same count and 3 change as intended (42373 e7f6922f and 42505 12957d6e, 0 to 6, bold; 42234 8dd067f4, 3 to 6, "###" with numbered lines inside premise 1); on 42373 the K-G10 items against the challenger go from 2 to 0. NOT SHOWN: no live run has gone through a bold or heading-numbered list; LIST NOT READ would print on none of the stored runs; the whole judgeBlock and ledger() of Panel Build and Build Independent Verdict were not run offline (their parts were). The grading: plan rev 0 PASS WITH N1, N2 (Wall 11824), applied in rev 1; build b1 FAIL on F1, the stored-rounds pass of the test had not been run (Wall 11918); regrade PASS WITH N3 after it ran (Wall 11928). N3: the six items-only changes on round d9924563 in the readers with no body-end stop are judged equal by rule, not by running their consumers, and the 761-list screen covered only the stop-bounded readers. Stated by W4 (Wall 11917, 11927): rev 0 had no style lock; a guard first put on LIB 998 was moved to 999; notes626.md first said d9924563 read byte-equal with the lock, which holds only for the stop-bounded readers. Open: two clean live runs in which a list path fires (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24); no revision of that is made by this row. REVISION (this row): the engine manual entry is WRITTEN, part 08.0 v299 to v320 (md5 e222253b, 52,600 characters), on the operator's press "Write it" at 05:14 CST 2026-11-25 on W3's card, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11970, 11975). objective_met stays 'in part': no live run has gone through a list path. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). FIRST RUN, PLAIN PATH ONLY. W4: both premise lists were read; the defender's list gave the six premises that assumption items 92 to 96 cite, and the challenger's list gave five; no "list not read" line was written. Both lists are numbered plainly ("1."), so the bold and heading path this ASK added is NOT EXERCISED, and LIST NOT READ was not printed. NOT CHECKED by W1: the "PREMISE COUNT: 5" line W4 cites. W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
